BSMTP  TITLE 'CUCCA VM NETWORK MAILER VERSION 1 - BSMTP DISTRIBUTION'
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*      MAILER -- Copyright (c) 1982,1987 Columbia University.         *
*    Program Property of the Trustees of Columbia University in the   *
*    City of New York.                                                *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
BSMTP    CSECT ,
* BSMTP  -
*
* This type 3 exit sends a single Batch Simple Mail Transfer Protocol
* (BSMTP) file to the named server with one RCPT TO: statement for
* each addressee provided in the chain of ACTADR blocks linked by the
* ACTCHN pointer.
*
* This is new code as of version 1.22 (12/2/85).  Alan Crosswell.
*
* The generated file will look like:
*  HELO domain
*  TICK message-id
** VERB ON               (removed)                               [1.24]
*  MAIL FROM: <sender>
*  RCPT TO: <recipient1>
*  RCPT TO: <recipient2>
*   . . .
*  RCPT TO: <recipientN>
*  DATA
*   [the mail file itself]
*  .
*  QUIT
*
* MEANING OF THE PARAMETER (RTPARM):                             [1.24]
*                                                                [1.24]
*  The parameter (if supplied) is the name of a variable which   [1.24]
*  has one of three meanings depending on what the first char of [1.24]
*  the parameter is:                                             [1.24]
*                                                                [1.24]
*  '@': The remaining 7 or less chars are the name of a variable [1.24]
*       that contains a RFC821 route-list which will be included [1.24]
*       in each RCPT TO.                                         [1.24]
*                                                                [1.24]
*  '%': The remaining chars are the name of a variable that con- [1.24]
*       tains a string to append to the end of the RCPT TO       [1.24]
*       address.  The usual at-sign in the address gets replaced [1.24]
*       by '%'.  This is sometimes called the routing kludge.    [1.24]
*       If the original address being modified included a route-list
*       (i.e. was of the form <@domain:user@host>) then the route-list
*       will be converted to use the '%' klidge also.
*                                                                [1.24]
*  else the parameter is the name of a variable that contains    [1.24]
*       the domain to put on the HELO command.  Normally,  the   [1.24]
*       HELO domain is one of:                                   [1.24]
*        o Local-domain variable if defined.                     [1.24]
*        o concatenation of Thisnode and RSCS-Domain variables.  [1.24]
*                                                                [1.24]
* EXAMPLES:                                                      [1.24]
*                                                                [1.24]
*  1. Passing the domain parameter:                              [1.24]
*     Domain=FOO.BAR.BAZ.EDU
*     . . .
*     XXX.ORG  *    *    BSMTP 3 Domain
*     This will cause a generated HELO line of:
*       HELO FOO.BAR.BAZ.EDU
*
*  2. Passing the route-list parameter:                          [1.24]
*     via20B=@CU20B.COLUMBIA.EDU                                 [1.24]
*     ...                                                        [1.24]
*     CUTC20.COLUMBIA.EDU  *  SMTPUSER BSMTP 3 =via20B           [1.24]
*     For "To: joe@CUTC20.COLUMBIA.EDU" it will generate:        [1.24]
*       RCPT TO:<@CU20B.COLUMBIA.EDU:joe@CUTC20.COLUMBIA.EDU>    [1.24]
*     For "To: <@xyz:joe@CUTC20.COLUMBIA.EDU>" it will generate:
*       RCPT TO:<@CU20B.COLUMBIA.EDU:joe@CUTC20.COLUMBIA.EDU>
*         if this node is 'xyz' otherwise it will generate:
*       RCPT TO:<@CU20B.COLUMBIA.EDU,@xyz:joe@CUTC20.COLUMBIA.EDU>
*                                                                [1.24]
*  3. Passing the kludge-route parameter:                        [1.24]
*     viaCSN=@CSNET-RELAY.ARPA                                   [1.24]
*     ...                                                        [1.24]
*     FOO.CSNET    *  GATEWAY BSMTP 3 %viaCSN                    [1.24]
*     For "To: joe@FOO.CSNET" it will generate:                  [1.24]
*       RCPT TO:<joe%FOO.CSNET@CSNET-RELAY.ARPA>                 [1.24]
*     For "To: <@xyz:joe@FOO.CSNET>" it will generate:
*       RCPT TO:<joe%FOO.CSNET@CSNET-RELAY.ARPA>
*         if this node is 'xyz' otherwise it will generate:
*       RCPT TO:<joe%FOO.CSNET%xyz@CSNET-RELAY.ARPA>
*                                                                [1.24]
* NOTES:                                                         [1.24]
*   1.  Clearly,  we need more than a single 8-char parameter.   [1.24]
*       You can't mix and match the three parameters for a single[1.24]
*       host.                                                    [1.24]
*   2.  Since this is a type 3 exit and may be called with a     [1.24]
*       list of recipients (ACTADR's),  multiple route-lists     [1.24]
*       and kludge-routes may be generated into the same BSMTP   [1.24]
*       transaction if the Outgoing/Domains table entries list   [1.24]
*       the same server node/userid.  This is entirely what you  [1.24]
*       want it to do (probably).                                [1.24]
*   3.  Mixing and matching '%'/'@' and non-'%'/'@' parameters   [1.24]
*       will probably not work right since the HELO domain is    [1.24]
*       picked from the first ACTADR->ROUTD in the list passed   [1.24]
*       while the '%'/'@' parameters are checked for each ACTADR [1.24]
*       (as they are used to generate the RCPTs).  This is not   [1.24]
*       a problem since there shouldn't even be a need overriding[1.24]
*       the "correct" HELO domain that you get already.          [1.24]
*   4.  xxx Maybe should add a Return-Path:  for % or @          [1.24]
*
* The MAIL FROM: name given will get the RSCS-DOMAIN tacked onto
* the end if there is not other domain already there.
PAB      DSECT ,
@MBLOK   DS    A             MAILBLOK base
@ACT     DS    A             ACTADR base
* REGISTER USAGE -
R0  EQU  0 -
R1  EQU  1 -
R2  EQU  2 -
R3  EQU  3 -
R4  EQU  4 -
R5  EQU  5 -
R6  EQU  6 -
R7  EQU  7 - MBOX base
R8  EQU  8 - Stack pointer
R9  EQU  9 - Stack length
R10 EQU 10 - ACTADR base
R11 EQU 11 - MAILBLOK base
R12 EQU 12 - program base
R13 EQU 13 - save area
R14 EQU 14 - linkage
R15 EQU 15 - linkage
         PRINT NOGEN
         BLOCKS ,
         MAILBLOK ,
         EJECT ,
BSMTP    CSECT ,
         USING BSMTP,R15          temp addr
         B     EYESKIP            around the eye-catcher
MYNAME   DC    CL8'BSMTP',CL8'&SYSDATE'
EYESKIP  DS    0H
         STM   R14,R12,12(R13)    save caller's registers
         LR    R12,R15            a better base
         DROP  R15                done with temp base
         USING BSMTP,R12          get perm base
         LA    R15,SAVE           point to my save area
         ST    R13,4(R15)         play the chain game
         ST    R15,8(R13)
         LR    R13,R15            set up my save pointer
         USING PAB,R1             get to the parms
         L     R11,@MBLOK         MAILBLOK base
         L     R10,@ACT           ACTADR base
         DROP  R1                 done with 'em
         USING MAILBLOK,R11       address the mailblok
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Point the punch in the right direction.  This exit is "smart" enough
* to handle a local or remote server (i.e. sent directly or via RSCS)
* If RSCS Version 2 was installed,  I wouldn't have to go thru the
* extra work!
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         USING ACTADR,R10         get the 1st ACTADR block
         L     R1,ACTRT           get the ROUTD
         USING ROUTD,R1           address it
         MVC   TAGNODE,RTROUTE    copy routd's node into tag cmd
         MVC   TAGUSER,RTUSER     copy routd's userid into tag cmd
         MVC   TAGWTR,RTUSER      dup it for the extwtr for jes
         CLC   RTROUTE,CPUSTR     is it for my node?
         BE    POINTLCL           point the punch locally then
         MVC   PUNUSER,RSCSNAME   get the rscs name into the buffer
         LA    R1,TAGPUN          point to tag punch command
         LA    R0,LTAGPUN         length of the command
         DC    X'83100008'        issue the tag command
         B     SPOOLIT            go issue the spool cmd
POINTLCL EQU   *                  now point the punch itself
         MVC   PUNUSER,RTUSER     move in the user from routd
         DROP  R1                 done with routd
SPOOLIT  EQU   *
         LA    R1,POINTPUN        the command
         LA    R0,LPOINT          length
         DC    X'83100008'        issue the spool command
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Set up the initial items: HELO, TICK, VERB, MAIL...
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         MVI   HELODOM,C' '                       Clear field  HELOCLR
         MVC   HELODOM+1(L'HELODOM-1),HELODOM     ...          HELOCLR
         L     R4,ACTRT           get the routd again
         USING ROUTD,R4           address it
         CLI   RTPARM,C' '        is the parm blank?
         BE    NOPARM             no parm,  the easy way out.
         CLI   RTPARM,C'@'        or '@' (for route-list)        [1.24]
         BE    NOPARM             so this parm is not domain     [1.24]
         LA    R4,RTPARM          point to the parm
         DROP  R4                 done with ROUTD
         LA    R1,8(R4)           end of parm
         MVI   TRAPTAB+C' ',X'FF' trap blanks
         TRT   0(8,R4),TRAPTAB    find end of string
         MVI   TRAPTAB+C' ',0     reset the trap table
         SR    R1,R4              get length of string
         LR    R5,R1              get into a better register
         L     R6,MAILPTAB        address of parm table
         L     R15,ATBLUK         address of table lookup
         CALL  (15),((R6),(R4),(R5),TWORK) find the parm
         LTR   R15,R15            not found?
         BNZ   NOPARM             ignore it
         LR    R5,R1              get a better copy of it
STUFFIT  EQU   *                  <- get here if Local-Host1 was set.
         SR    R1,R1              zero it for IC
         IC    R1,0(R5)           length
         C     R1,=A(L'HELODOM)   room for it?
         BNL   OVERFLOW           doesn't fit
         BCTR  R1,0               -1 for execute
         EX    R1,MOVEDOM         MVC HELODOM(0),1(R5)
         B     HADPARM            skip over the noparm stuff
NOPARM   EQU   *                  here if no parameter
         ICM   R5,B'1111',LCLHOST1 See if Local-Host1 was set
         BNZ   STUFFIT            -> go back up and stuff it in  [1.24]
         MVC   HELODOM(8),CPUSTR  copy in rscs node name
         CLC   RSCSDOM,=A(0)      was a domain given?
         BE    HADPARM            no domain,  cpustr is enuf
         L     R1,CPUSLEN         get the actual length of node name
         LA    R2,HELODOM(R1)     where to start copying
         LA    R3,HELODOM+L'HELODOM address of end of buffer
         L     R4,RSCSDOM         ptr to string
         SR    R5,R5              get a zero
         IC    R5,0(R4)           get domain string length
         LA    R0,0(R2,R5)        address of end
         CR    R0,R3              see if it will fit
         BNL   OVERFLOW           no room - croak
         BCTR  R5,0               -1 for execute
         EX    R5,COPYDEF         MVC 0(0,R2),1(R4)
HADPARM  EQU   *
         PUNCHC HELO,ERROR=PUNERR punch the HELO record
         MVC   TICKID,MAILFTXT    message id number
         PUNCHC TICK,ERROR=PUNERR punch the TICK
******** PUNCHC VERB,ERROR=PUNERR punch the VERB                 [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* MAIL FROM:<sender> is a little more work...
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         TM    MAILFLG2,MFLG2NLF  is it "MAIL FROM:<>"?
         BO    NULLFROM           --> propagate that fact
         L     R6,MAILSFLD        sender fieldd
         USING FIELDD,R6          address it
         L     R6,FIPARS          point to mbox
         DROP  R6                 done with fieldd
         USING MBOX,R6          use the mbox now
         LA    R2,MAILFROM        address of buffer for userid
         LA    R3,L'MAILFROM(R2)  length of it
         MVI   MAILFROM,C' '      blank it out
         MVC   MAILFROM+1(L'MAILFROM-1),MAILFROM propagate the blanks
         ST    R6,GENMBMBX              Save address of MBOX dsect
         ST    R2,GENMBSTK              Update stack address
         MVC   GENSTKSZ,=A(L'MAILFROM)  Update stack length
         CALL  GENMBOX,(GENMBMBX,GENMBSTR,GENMBSTL,GENMBSTK,GENSTKSZ)
         LTR   R15,R15            did it fit?
         BNZ   OVERFLOW           didn't fit!
         A     R2,GENMBSTL        update buffer pointer
         CLC   RSCSDOM,=A(0)      do we have a RSCS-domain?
         BE    NODEF              no - don't tack one on then
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Check to see if a domain name is already there (more than 1 token
* in the mailbox domain list).  If not, tack on our default domain
* name on the assumption that the user is in the same domain as us
* (since otherwise they would have included a fully qualified domain
* name).
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         CLC   MBXDCNT,=F'1'      More than 1 token?
         BH    NODEF              ---> Yes, no tack on
         ICM   R4,B'1111',RSCSDOM Get the string pointer
         BZ    NODEF              ---> No RSCS-domain, leave alone
         BCTR  R2,0               backup over the ending '>'
         SR    R1,R1              get a zero
         IC    R1,0(R4)           get the string length
         LA    R0,0(R1,R2)        address of end after copy
         CR    R0,R3              see if it will fit
         BNL   OVERFLOW           nope - overflow
         BCTR  R1,0               decrement for executed mvc
         EX    R1,COPYDEF         MVC 0(0,R2),1(R4)
         LA    R2,1(R1,R2)        bump output pointer
         CR    R2,R3              room for the ">"?
         BNL   OVERFLOW           didn't fit
         MVI   0(R2),C'>'         end of the mail from
NODEF    EQU   *
         LR    R15,R2             Copy buffer pointer
         S     R15,=A(MAIL)       Compute length
         C     R15,=F'80'         Longer than 80?
         BH    NODEF2             ---> Yes
         PUNCHC MAIL,ERROR=PUNERR punch the MAIL FROM: line
         DROP  R6                 done with MBOX
         B     OVERNULL           --> skip null "from" code
         SPACE 1
NODEF2   EQU   *                  Here if length > 80
         MVC   TWORK(1),MAIL+79      Save value
         MVI   MAIL+79,X'15'         Put in NL character
         PUNCHC MAIL,ERROR=PUNERR    Punch the MAIL FROM: line
         MVC   MAIL+79(1),TWORK      Restore char
         PUNCHC MAIL+79,ERROR=PUNERR Punch the continuation
         B     OVERNULL
         SPACE 1
NULLFROM EQU   *                  <-- here for MAIL FROM:<>
         PUNCHC 'MAIL FROM:<>',ERROR=PUNERR
OVERNULL EQU   *                  <-- here when skipping over
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Iterrate through the list of ACTADR's via ACTCHN.  For each one,
* generate a RCPT TO: line.
* First, see if they specified a route-list in RTPARM            [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
ACTLOOP  EQU   *                  top of loop to go thru the chain
         MVI   ATPCT,C'@'         set default                    [1.24]
         XC    ADDRNODE,ADDRNODE  set default
         L     R4,ACTRT           get the current routd          [1.24]
         USING ROUTD,R4           address it                     [1.24]
         CLI   RTPARM,C' '        is the parm blank?             [1.24]
         BE    NOPARM1            no parm,  the easy way out.    [1.24]
         CLI   RTPARM,C'%'        is it a kludge-list?           [1.24]
         BE    PARMPCT                                           [1.24]
         CLI   RTPARM,C'@'        start with '@' for route-list? [1.24]
         BNE   NOPARM1            no, it was a domain(above)     [1.24]
         B     PARMAT             skip this:                     [1.24]
PARMPCT  EQU   *                  '%' seen                       [1.24]
         MVI   ATPCT,C'%'         remember it.                   [1.24]
PARMAT   EQU   *                                                 [1.24]
         LA    R4,RTPARM+1        point to the parm              [1.24]
         DROP  R4                 done with ROUTD                [1.24]
         LA    R1,7(R4)           end of parm                    [1.24]
         MVI   TRAPTAB+C' ',X'FF' trap blanks                    [1.24]
         TRT   0(7,R4),TRAPTAB    find end of string             [1.24]
         MVI   TRAPTAB+C' ',0     reset the trap table           [1.24]
         SR    R1,R4              get length of string           [1.24]
         LR    R5,R1              get into a better register     [1.24]
         L     R6,MAILPTAB        address of parm table          [1.24]
         L     R15,ATBLUK         address of table lookup        [1.24]
         CALL  (15),((R6),(R4),(R5),TWORK) find the parm         [1.24]
         LTR   R15,R15            not found?                     [1.24]
         BNZ   NOPARM1            ignore it                      [1.24]
         LR    R5,R1              get a better copy of it        [1.24]
         SR    R1,R1              zero it for IC                 [1.24]
         IC    R1,0(R5)           length                         [1.24]
         ST    R5,PARMSTR         parm string pointer for later  [1.24]
         ST    R1,PARMLEN         (maybe)                        [1.24]
         CLI   ATPCT,C'%'         is it % rather than @?         [1.24]
         BE    NOPARM1            yes, skip this junk:           [1.24]
         LM    R8,R9,STACKP       get stack pointer
         S     R9,=A(2*NODSIZ+TOKSIZ)   Will 2 NODEs + 1 TOKEND fit?
         BL    OVERFLOW                 ---> No
         ST    R8,ADDRNODE        Save for call to ADDROUTE
         XC    0(2*NODSIZ+TOKSIZ,R8),0(R8) Zero NODEs and TOKEND
         LA    R15,NODSIZ(,R8)          Point to second NODE
         ST    R15,NODDOWN-NODE(R8)     Connect level 1 and level 2
         LA    R8,NODSIZ(,R15)          Set base for TOKEND
         ST    R8,NODDOWN-NODE(R15)     Point level 2 NODE to TOKEND
         USING TOKEND,R8
         LA    R15,1(,R5)         Point to parm string
         CLI   0(R15),C'@'        Does it begin with an '@'?
         BNE   NOPARM0A           ---> No, all ok
         LA    R15,1(,R15)        Point past '@'
         BCTR  R1,0               Fix up field length
NOPARM0A DS    0H
         ST    R15,TOKPTR         Put ptr in TOKEND
         ST    R1,TOKLEN          Put length in TOKEND
         MVI   TOKTYPE,TOKATM     Call it an atom
         DROP  R8
         LA    R8,TOKSIZ(,R8)     Bump stack pointer
         STM   R8,R9,STACKP       Save updated pointer and length
NOPARM1  EQU   *                  here if no parameter           [1.24]
         L     R7,ACTMBOX         GET MBOX BLOCK
         USING MBOX,R7
         CLC   ADDRNODE,=F'0'     Have a routelist to add?
         BE    NOPARM1A           ---> No
         ST    R7,ADDRMBOX        Save MBOX address in plist
         CALL  ADDROUTE,(ADDRMBOX,ADDRNODE)
         LTR   R15,R15            Successful?
*        BNZ   ???                ---> What do I do here?
NOPARM1A DS    0H
         LA    R2,RCPTTO          Address of buffer for userid
         MVI   RCPTTO,C' '        fill with blanks first         [1.24]
         MVC   RCPTTO+1(L'RCPTTO-1),RCPTTO
         ST    R7,GENMBMBX              Save address of MBOX dsect
         ST    R2,GENMBSTK              Update stack address
         MVC   GENSTKSZ,=A(L'RCPTTO)    Update stack length
         CALL  GENMBOX,(GENMBMBX,GENMBSTR,GENMBSTL,GENMBSTK,GENSTKSZ)
         LTR   R15,R15            Successful?
         BNZ   OVERFLOW           didn't fit!
         A     R2,GENMBSTL        update buffer pointer
         CLI   ATPCT,C'%'         is it a kludge-route?          [1.24]
         BNE   NOPARM2            nope, all done.                [1.24]
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
*  The '%' kludge is handled as follows:
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
*
*  The last '@' in the address will be replaced with a '%' and the
*  new domain (supplied as the value of the parm) is placed behind
*  the string created by GENMBOX.
*
         L     R5,PARMSTR         get ptr back from above        [1.24]
         L     R1,PARMLEN         and length of it               [1.24]
         LA    R0,1(R1,R2)        where end of string would be   [1.24]
         C     R0,=A(RCPTTO+L'RCPTTO)  compare to end of buffer
         BNL   OVERFLOW           not enough room                [1.24]
         BCTR  R2,0               Back up over '>'
         LR    R15,R2             Copy pointer
KLUDGE01 EQU   *
         BCTR  R15,0              Backup 1 character
         C     R15,=A(RCPTTO)     At start of string
         BE    KLUDGE99           ---> Yes, all done
         CLI   0(R15),C'@'        This last '@'?
         BNE   KLUDGE01           ---> No
         MVI   0(R15),C'%'        Replace with '%'
KLUDGE99 EQU   *
         BCTR  R1,0               -1 for executed move           [1.24]
         EX    R1,MOVER2          MVC 0(0,R2),0(R5)              [1.24]
         LA    R2,1(R1,R2)        update the pointer             [1.24]
         MVI   0(R2),C'>'         Put closing '>' back in
         LA    R2,1(,R2)          Update the pointer
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         SPACE 1
NOPARM2  EQU   *                  <- here if no kludge-route     [1.24]
         LR    R15,R2             Copy buffer ptr
         S     R15,=A(RCPT)       Compute length
         C     R15,=F'80'         Longer than 80?
         BH    NOPARM3            ---> Yes
         PUNCHC RCPT,ERROR=PUNERR punch the MAIL FROM: line
         B     NOPARM99           --> Continue
         SPACE 1
NOPARM3  EQU   *
         MVC   TWORK(1),RCPT+79   Save value of this char
         MVI   RCPT+79,X'15'      Put in NL character
         PUNCHC RCPT,ERROR=PUNERR punch the MAIL FROM: line
         MVC   RCPT+79(1),TWORK   Restore char
         PUNCHC RCPT+79,ERROR=PUNERR Punch the second line
         SPACE 1
NOPARM99 EQU   *
         ICM   R10,B'1111',ACTCHN get next ACTADR in the list
         BNZ   ACTLOOP            there is another; back to top
         DROP  R7                 done with MBOX
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* done with RCPT's.  Now send the DATA
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         PUNCHC DATA,ERROR=PUNERR send the data
         OI    MAILFLG1,MFLG1DOT  do dot quoting
         L     R15,APUNHDR
         CALL  (15),((R11))       send the header
         LTR   R15,R15
         BNZ   RET
         L     R15,APUNTXT
         CALL  (15),((R11))       send the text
         LTR   R15,R15
         BNZ   RET
         PUNCHC ENDDATA,ERROR=PUNERR end the data
         PUNCHC QUIT,ERROR=PUNERR end the "session"
         L     R15,APUNCLS        close the punch
         CALL  (15),((R11))
         LTR   R15,R15
         BNZ   RET
         LA    R4,CPUSTR          some sort of message??
         LOG   BSM034,(CA,TAGUSER,CA,TAGNODE)
RET      EQU   *
         NI    MAILFLG1,255-MFLG1DOT turn off dot quoting
         L     R13,4(R13)
         L     R14,12(R13)
         LM    R0,R12,20(R13)
         BR    R14
         EJECT ,
* Executed instructions
         SPACE 1
COPY     MVC   0(0,R2),0(R5)      executed instr
COPYDEF  MVC   0(0,R2),1(R4)      executed mvc
TRAPDOT  TRT   0(0,R4),TRAPTAB    executed trt
MOVEDOM  MVC   HELODOM(0),1(R5)   executed mvc
MOVERTL  MVC   RCPTTO(0),1(R5)     "                             [1.24]
MOVEBLK  MVC   1(0,R2),0(R2)       "                             [1.24]
MOVER2   MVC   0(0,R2),1(R5)       "                             [1.24]
         SPACE 1
PARMSTR  DS    A                  ptr to parameter string value  [1.24]
PARMLEN  DS    F                  length of above                [1.24]
ATPCT    DS    C                  '@' or '%'                     [1.24]
         SPACE 1
ADDRMBOX DS    A(0)               Address of MBOX to which to add
*                                   new route-list part
ADDRNODE DS    A(0)               Address of NODE for route-list
*                                   being added
         SPACE 1
GENMBSTK DS    A(0)               Stack area for MBOX expansion
GENSTKSZ DS    F'0'               Size of stack area
GENMBMBX DS    A(0)               Address of MBOX dsect
GENMBSTR DS    A(0)               Address of generated MBOX string
GENMBSTL DS    F'0'               Length of generated string
         SPACE ,
OVERFLOW DS    0H                 overflow error
         LOG   BSM026,(CA,MYNAME) error message
         LA    R15,4              set error status
OVERPUR  EQU   *
         LA    R1,=C'SP PUN PURGE' purge what's been punched so far
         LA    R0,12              length
         DC    X'83100008'        diagnose 8
         B     RET                and return
         SPACE ,
PUNERR   DS    0H                 punch error
         LOG   BSM026,(CA,MYNAME)
         LA    R15,12             fatal error
         B     OVERPUR            do the purge stuff
         LTORG ,
SAVE     DS    18F                save area
HELO     DC    CL80' '            a helo message
         ORG   HELO               org back to it
         DC    CL5'HELO '         the constant part
HELODOM  DC    CL75' '            the domain that gets filled in
         ORG   ,
VERB     DC    CL80'VERB ON'      the verb message
TICK     DC    CL80' '            the tick message
         ORG   TICK
         DC    CL5'TICK '
TICKID   DC    CL4'0000'          the id number
         ORG   ,
MAIL     DC    CL160' '           the mail message
         ORG   MAIL
         DC    CL10'MAIL FROM:'
MAILFROM DC    CL150' '           space for the userid
         ORG   ,
RCPT     DC    CL160' '           rcpt message
         ORG   RCPT
         DC    CL8'RCPT TO:'
RCPTTO   DC    CL152' '           space for the address
         ORG   ,
DATA     DC    CL80'DATA'         data message
ENDDATA  DC    CL80'.'            end of data message
QUIT     DC    CL80'QUIT'         quit message
POINTPUN DC    C'SP PUN CLASS M TO '
PUNUSER  DC    CL8' '
LPOINT   EQU   *-POINTPUN
TAGPUN   DC    C'TAG DEV PUN '
TAGNODE  DC    CL8' ',C' '
TAGUSER  DC    CL8' ',C' 50 W='
TAGWTR   DC    CL8' '
LTAGPUN  EQU   *-TAGPUN
TWORK    DS    512C
         END   BSMTP
